# Response headers for cianporteous.com.
#
# This file is only read at the ROOT of the assets directory (./static, per
# wrangler.toml). A copy in a subdirectory is silently ignored — which is what
# happened to static/clonskeagh/_headers, whose cache rules never once applied.
# If you add rules, they belong here.

# ---- temporarily hidden from search engines -------------------------------
#
# X-Robots-Tag rather than a robots.txt Disallow, and deliberately so: robots.txt
# only blocks crawling, and a crawler that is not allowed to fetch the page never
# sees a noindex on it, so pages already in the index linger there as bare links.
# The two mechanisms work against each other. This header is the one that
# actually takes a page out of an index, and it covers the JSON and assets as
# well as the HTML.
#
# For an immediate drop rather than a wait for the next crawl, pair this with
# Google Search Console -> Removals -> Temporary removal (about six months) and
# Bing Webmaster Tools -> Block URLs. This header is what keeps it out once
# those expire.
#
# TO UNDO: delete the two lines below and redeploy, then request reindexing in
# Search Console. The config change takes effect immediately; getting back into
# the index afterwards takes days to weeks.
# ---- everything else ------------------------------------------------------
#
# nosniff: trust the declared Content-Type instead of inspecting the bytes and
# guessing. Little to defend here — every file on this site is one we wrote,
# there are no uploads — but it costs nothing.
#
# no-referrer rather than the usual strict-origin-when-cross-origin, which is
# already the browser default and so would change nothing. The game's radio
# opens connections to twenty third-party stream servers, and each request
# would otherwise announce cianporteous.com in their access logs. This sends
# nothing at all. The risk with no-referrer is servers that use referrer-based
# hotlink protection, but all twenty stations were verified with curl, which
# sends no referrer, and every one of them returned audio.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
